{"schema":1,"locale":"zh-Hans","created_at":"2026-11-28T11:26:06.647Z","entries":{"docs-7.24\u0000## Bridge Hardware Offloading":"## 网桥硬件卸载","docs-7.24\u0000## Multicast Table":"## 组播表","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/remote-cap **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Directory":"## caps-man/remote-cap \n**包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** 目录","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/remote-cap/set-identity **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Command":"## caps-man/remote-cap/set-identity \n**Package：** wireless-rep\n**Type：** Command","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/remote-cap/upgrade **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Command":"## caps-man/remote-cap/upgrade \n**软件包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** Command","docs-7.24\u0000## caps-man/security **Package:** wireless-rep **Type:** Directory":"## caps-man/security \n**包：** wireless-rep\n**类型：** 目录","docs-7.24\u0000## certificate/acme-renew **Type:** Command":"## certificate/acme-renew \n**类型：** 命令","docs-7.24\u0000## certificate/add-acme **Type:** Command":"## certificate/add-acme \n**类型：** 命令","docs-7.24\u0000## certificate/add-scep **Type:** Command":"## certificate/add-scep \n**类型：** 命令","docs-7.24\u0000## certificate/builtin **Type:** Directory":"## certificate/builtin \n**类型：** 目录","docs-7.24\u0000## certificate/card-reinstall **Type:** Command":"## certificate/card-reinstall \n**类型：** 命令","docs-7.24\u0000## certificate/card-verify **Type:** Command":"## certificate/card-verify \n**类型：** 命令","docs-7.24\u0000## certificate/create-certificate-request **Type:** Command":"## certificate/create-certificate-request \n**类型：** 命令","docs-7.24\u0000### Static entries":"### 静态条目","docs-7.24\u0000:::danger Certain bridge and Ethernet port properties are directly related to switch chip settings. Changing such properties can trigger a **switch chip reset**, temporarily disabling all Ethernet ports. This must be taken into account whenever changing properties in production environments. Such properties include DHCP Snooping, IGMP Snooping, VLAN filtering, L2MTU, Flow Control, and others. The exact settings that can trigger a switch chip reset depend on the device's model. :::":":::danger\n某些网桥和以太网端口属性与交换芯片设置直接相关。更改此类属性可能触发 **switch chip reset**，临时禁用所有以太网端口。在生产环境中更改属性时必须考虑这一点。此类属性包括 DHCP Snooping、IGMP Snooping、VLAN filtering、L2MTU、Flow Control 等。可能触发交换芯片复位的确切设置取决于设备型号。\n:::","docs-7.24\u0000:::warning [CRS1xx/2xx series switches](LINK) support multiple hardware offloaded bridges per switch chip. All other devices support only one. Use `hw=yes/no` under `/interface/bridge/port` to select which bridge uses hardware offloading. :::":":::warning\n[CRS1xx/2xx series switches](/docs/7.24/bridging-and-switching/crs1xx-and-2xx-series-switches#multiple-switch-groups) 支持每个交换芯片多个硬件卸载网桥。所有其他设备仅支持一个。在 `/interface/bridge/port` 下使用 `hw=yes/no` 选择哪个网桥使用硬件卸载。\n:::","docs-7.24\u0000A packet that is received by one of the ports always passes through the switch logic first. Switch logic decides which ports the packet should be going to - usually based on the destination MAC address. Hardware-forwarded packets will not be visible to RouterOS(only statistics will show that a packet has passed through). This is because the packet was already processed by the switch chip and never reached the CPU.":"端口接收到的数据包始终先经过交换逻辑。交换逻辑决定数据包应发往哪些端口，通常基于目标 MAC 地址。硬件转发的数据包对 RouterOS 不可见（只有统计信息会显示数据包已经通过）。这是因为数据包已由交换芯片处理，从未到达 CPU。","docs-7.24\u0000For example, to create a static MDB entry for multicast group 229.10.10.10 on ports ether2 and ether3 on VLAN 10, use the command below:":"例如，要在 VLAN 10 的端口 ether2 和 ether3 上为组播组 229.10.10.10 创建静态 MDB 条目，请使用以下命令：","docs-7.24\u0000In case a certain IPv6 multicast group does not need to be snooped and it is desired for it to be flooded on all ports and VLANs, it is possible to create a static MDB entry on all VLANs and ports, including the bridge interface itself. Use the command below to create a static MDB entry for multicast group ff02::2 on all VLANs and ports(modify the `ports` setting for your particular setup):":"如果某个 IPv6 组播组不需要被侦听，并且希望在所有端口和 VLAN 上泛洪，则可以在所有 VLAN 和端口（包括网桥接口本身）上创建静态 MDB 条目。使用以下命令为组播组 ff02::2 在所有 VLAN 和端口上创建静态 MDB 条目（根据你的具体配置修改 `ports` 设置）：","docs-7.24\u0000It is possible to switch multiple ports together if a device has a built-in switch chip. While a bridge is a software feature that will consume CPU's resources, the bridge hardware offloading will allow you to use the built-in switch chip to forward packets at wire speed. This allows you to achieve higher throughput if configured correctly.":"如果设备内置交换芯片，则可以将多个端口切换在一起。网桥是软件功能，会消耗 CPU 资源，而网桥硬件卸载允许使用内置交换芯片以线速转发数据包。正确配置后，这可以实现更高的吞吐量。","docs-7.24\u0000Note that packets addressed to link-local multicast groups 224.0.0.0/24 and ff02::1 are exceptions to this behavior - these addresses are always flooded to all ports and VLANs without restriction, as they are used for network protocol operations.":"请注意，发往链路本地组播组 224.0.0.0/24 和 ff02::1 的数据包是此行为的例外——这些地址始终不受限制地泛洪到所有端口和 VLAN，因为它们用于网络协议运行。","docs-7.24\u0000Packets can be forwarded to the CPU via the switch CPU port for management access, routing, firewall rules, or traffic control. This requires configuration specific to your device and use case. Check the manual page for your specific device:":"数据包可以通过交换 CPU 端口转发到 CPU，用于管理访问、路由、防火墙规则或流量控制。这需要针对你的设备和用例进行特定配置。请查看对应设备的手册页面：","docs-7.24\u0000Since RouterOS version 7.7, it is possible to create static MDB entries for IPv4 and IPv6 multicast groups.":"从 RouterOS 7.7 版本开始，可以为 IPv4 和 IPv6 组播组创建静态 MDB 条目。","docs-7.24\u0000The Multicast Table displays multicast group membership information learned through IGMP/MLD snooping. When IGMP/MLD snooping is enabled on a bridge, the device actively monitors IGMP/MLD network communications to build a Multicast Database(MDB) of active multicast groups and their subscribed ports members. The bridge then uses this information to intelligently forward multicast traffic only to ports where interested receivers devices are connected, rather than flooding all ports with multicast traffic.":"Multicast Table 显示通过 IGMP/MLD snooping 学习到的组播组成员信息。当网桥上启用 IGMP/MLD snooping 时，设备会主动监控 IGMP/MLD 网络通信，以构建包含活动组播组及其已订阅端口成员的 Multicast Database（MDB）。随后，网桥使用此信息智能地将组播流量仅转发到连接了感兴趣接收设备的端口，而不是向所有端口泛洪组播流量。","docs-7.24\u0000The following tables list which bridge features are supported with hardware offloading(✓) or disable hardware offloading(✗) for each switch chip type:":"下表列出了每种交换芯片类型支持硬件卸载（✓）或禁用硬件卸载（✗）的网桥功能：","docs-7.24\u0000To view the current multicast database entries table, use the `print` command in the multicast database submenu.":"要查看当前组播数据库条目表，请在组播数据库子菜单中使用 `print` 命令。","docs-7.24\u0000| Property | Description | | :-- | :-- | | **bridge**(*name*; Default:) | The bridge interface to which the MDB entry is going to be assigned. | | **disabled**(*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | Disables or enables the static MDB entry. | | **group**(*ipv4 \\| ipv6 \\| MAC address*; Default:) | The IPv4, IPv6 or MAC multicast address. Static entries for link-local multicast groups 224.0.0.0/24 and ff02::1 cannot be created, as these packets are always flooded on all ports and VLANs. | | **interface**(*name*; Default:) | The list of bridge ports to which the multicast group will be forwarded. | | **vid**(*integer: 1..4094*; Default:) | The VLAN ID on which the MDB entry will be created only applies when `vlan-filtering` is enabled. When VLAN ID is not specified, the entry will work in shared-VLAN mode and dynamically apply to all defined VLAN IDs for particular ports. |":"| 属性 | 说明 |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| **bridge** (*name*; Default: ) | 要将 MDB 条目分配到的网桥接口。 |\n| **disabled** (*yes \\| no*; Default: **no**) | 禁用或启用静态 MDB 条目。 |\n| **group** (*ipv4 \\| ipv6 \\| MAC address*; Default: ) | IPv4、IPv6 或 MAC 组播地址。无法为链路本地组播组 224.0.0.0/24 和 ff02::1 创建静态条目，因为这些数据包始终会在所有端口和 VLAN 上泛洪。 |\n| **interface** (*name*; Default: ) | 要将组播组转发到的网桥端口列表。 |\n| **vid** (*integer: 1..4094*; Default: ) | 创建 MDB 条目所在的 VLAN ID，仅在启用 `vlan-filtering` 时适用。未指定 VLAN ID 时，该条目将在 shared-VLAN 模式下工作，并动态应用于特定端口的所有已定义 VLAN ID。 |","docs-7.24\u0000| Property | Description | | :-- | :-- | | <strong>bridge</strong>(<em>read-only: name</em>) | Shows the bridge interface the entry belongs to. | | <strong>group</strong>(*read-only:*ipv4 | ipv6 | | <strong>on-interface</strong>(<em>read-only: name</em>) | Shows the bridge ports which are subscribed to the multicast group. | | <strong>vid</strong>(<em>read-only: integer</em>) | Shows the VLAN ID for the multicast group, only applies when <span className=\"ros-background-accent-green-bolder\"><code>vlan-filtering</code></span> is enabled. |":"| 属性 | 说明 |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| <strong>bridge</strong> (<em>read-only: name</em>) | 显示该条目所属的网桥接口。 |\n| <strong>group</strong> (*read-only:*ipv4 | ipv6 |\n| <strong>on-interface</strong> (<em>read-only: name</em>) | 显示已订阅该组播组的网桥端口。 |\n| <strong>vid</strong> (<em>read-only: integer</em>) | 显示组播组的 VLAN ID，仅在启用 <span className=\"ros-background-accent-green-bolder\"><code>vlan-filtering</code></span> 时适用。 |"}}
